Author: Jack Sumner <jack@jacksumner.com>
Date:   Sun May 17 13:14:09 2026 -0400

    polymarket: watchlist weekly refresh — Cloudflare 403 retry + --merge + systemd timer
    
    Unblocks the P2 weekly cron for `agent_state(polymarket_copy_trader,
    watch_only_whales)`. The 14:43 UTC prod seed crashed at chunk 1163 with
    HTTP 403 from gamma-api (Cloudflare rate-limited the Azure VM IP, shared
    with PCT live + polymarket_arbitrage live). Without these three changes
    the weekly Sunday cron will fail the same way every week.
    
    1. _get_json: exponential backoff (30/60/120/240/300s, ~6 attempts) on
       403+cf-ray-marker responses. Terminal failure raises the existing
       PolymarketRateLimitError. Non-Cloudflare 403s are NOT retried — only
       the rate-limit interstitial signature triggers retry.
    
    2. fetch_market_resolutions: per-chunk swallow on PolymarketRateLimitError.
       Failed chunks fall through to the existing not_found sentinel so the
       caller still gets a complete dict; sweep continues with partial
       coverage instead of aborting (compute_polymarket_stats already handles
       not_found resolutions cleanly).
    
    3. seed_polymarket_watchlist_deep:
       - --merge: union freshly-computed top-N with existing slot; existing
         entries' included_iso preserved (so we can track observation
         duration), per-wallet stats take fresh values.
       - --max-total N: cap merged list size by realized_pnl_usdc desc;
         prevents unbounded growth.
       - Merge stats reported in summary + human print.
    
    4. systemd timer: trading-corp-pm-watchlist-deep.{service,timer}
       weekly Sunday 13:00 UTC, RandomizedDelaySec=900, ExecStart with
       --merge --max-total 100. Slot between daily 12:00 UTC Kalshi
       stats-refresh and Sunday 14:00 UTC Kalshi deep-scan to avoid
       concurrent bulk-API load.
    
    12 new tests; 52 existing Polymarket tests pass.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

